  "name": "Mantid",
  "description": "A massive insectoid predator standing taller than most humans, the mantid is a patient and lethal ambush hunter. Its bladed forelegs can slice through leather and bone with terrifying speed, and its compound eyes track movement in almost every direction. Mantids are solitary territorial creatures, often found in dense forests or overgrown ruins where their natural camouflage makes them nearly invisible until they strike.",
  "tactics": "The mantid relies on ambush tactics, using its camouflage to remain hidden until prey wanders close. It opens with a Lunging Strike to close distance and immediately follows with Raptorial Strike. If surrounded, it uses Reaping Sweep to clear space. It fights until reduced to roughly a third of its health, then attempts to flee by climbing to safety.",
